From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: dwrite: a glyph outside a run's bounds is clipped, not written past the bitmap

CreateAlphaTexture blitted each glyph into the run's bitmap at its bounding
box without checking it against the run's bounds. When the two disagreed
the write went past the buffer and crashed. Paint.NET's panels hit this at
start, intermittently. Only the part of the glyph inside the bounds is now
copied.

Gate: none that fails reliably (the crash was intermittent); dwrite:font
and dwrite:layout give the same results before and after.
---
--- a/dlls/dwrite/font.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
@@ -6231,6 +6231,33 @@
 
         OffsetRect(bbox, analysis->origins[i].x, analysis->origins[i].y);
 
+        /* A glyph can reach outside the bounds the run was measured with
+         * (by rounding, or under a transform); only its part inside them is
+         * blitted. */
+        if (bbox->left < analysis->bounds.left || bbox->top < analysis->bounds.top
+                || bbox->right > analysis->bounds.right || bbox->bottom > analysis->bounds.bottom)
+        {
+            RECT clipped;
+            int skip_x, skip_y;
+
+            if (!IntersectRect(&clipped, bbox, &analysis->bounds))
+                continue;
+            skip_x = clipped.left - bbox->left;
+            skip_y = clipped.top - bbox->top;
+            if (is_1bpp && skip_x)
+            {
+                /* 1bpp rows cannot start mid-byte here; drop such glyphs' clipped columns later */
+                skip_x = 0;
+                clipped.left = bbox->left;
+                if (clipped.left < analysis->bounds.left)
+                    continue;
+            }
+            src += skip_y * glyph_bitmap.pitch + skip_x;
+            *bbox = clipped;
+            width = bbox->right - bbox->left;
+            height = bbox->bottom - bbox->top;
+        }
+
         /* blit to analysis bitmap */
         dst = get_pixel_ptr(analysis->bitmap, analysis->texture_type, bbox, &analysis->bounds);
 
